  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Schools and families judge a tool by how useful and respectful it is. They check whether it leads to action.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is turning an answer into a next step that can be tested.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and career guidance questionnaire for students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can draft questions and summarise answers. Routine summarising shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, care with people and follow-up hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and organise; later, hold the conversations yourself.
  </p>

